I've heard about this, too--in particular, I've heard of an 
experiment in which long-lived and short-lived fish were produced
simply by respectively breeding them from younger or older
parents. In not very many generations, the the fish from younger
parents were living twice as long as those from older parents.

On the other hand, I haven't seen a citation--has anyone
else heard of this? Care to try it for yourself in your home
aquarium?

